  "verification_scope": "All source text structurally inventoried; GFG descriptive pp11–14 and conversion/timingp5 visually checked, GateForump11 visually compared. Additional mirrors inspected for numbering gap. Not a full symbol-by-symbol equivalence certification. Both main files preserve same page distribution. No solutions copied/authored.",
  "discrepancies": [
    {
      "question": "scope3–5",
      "note": "Both CS reproductions jump2.10→6.1. The absent original groups3–5 are unresolved in scope, not certified missing CS questions: a separately retrieved EC1993 reproduction has identical1/2 mathematics, then3 Physics and4/5 Section F electrical topics. This suggests shared Part I sections, but no original1993 CS selection instructions were located. Do not import EC questions as CS without verification."
    },
    {
      "question": "6.2",
      "note": "Both CS reproductions refer to a state-machine figure but show no dedicated figure between6.1 and6.3. The neighboring figures concern different questions. Treat essential diagram availability as unresolved; do not invent its gate type."
    },
    {
      "question": "6.5",
      "note": "Two explicitly labelled conversion parts(a)/(b) are separate leaves with shared2marks. Base H in(b) denotes the printed desired base; explain any interpretation."
    },
    {
      "question": "6.8",
      "note": "Interrupt timing diagram includes10microseconds response delay while main program still executes, then10 saving,80 service,10 restoration. Inspect timing boundaries, not OCR concatenated numbers."
    },
    {
      "question": "7.1–7.3",
      "note": "All three share the Pascal PARAM listing onp6. Preserve local/global m shadowing and reference/value parameter modes; OCR punctuation is unreliable."
    },
    {
      "question": "7.5",
      "note": "Both program reproductions write ln(ptr) and dereference nil; do not silently repair Pascal typing or output syntax when discussing possible compile-time versus runtime behavior."
    },
    {
      "question": "8.5",
      "note": "Partial-order options contain confusing asymmetry/antisymmetry/reflexivity wording. Preserve actual option text and distinguish strict versus non-strict order conventions."
    },
    {
      "question": "9",
      "note": "Implementing all binary Boolean functions using only half adders requires careful treatment of constants/tied inputs. The source gives no explicit constant-supply convention; do not silently assume one."
    },
    {
      "question": "12",
      "note": "The four boxed code blanks A–D form one program-completion question, kept as one leaf with all four outputs required."
    },
    {
      "question": "13",
      "note": "Both GFG/Examrace p11 and GateForum p11 omit inserted d from the requested output sequence. Insert-before-X is an explicit intended interpretation, not a source-verified correction."
    },
    {
      "question": "15",
      "note": "Both printed recursive bubblesort listings omit a terminating base-case guard and contain temp assignment punctuation typo. A finite recurrence answer must state the conventional termination assumption rather than claiming literal code terminates."
    },
    {
      "question": "17",
      "note": "Both sources give21 persons,9 vegetable,10 fish,7 eggs,5 all three, without saying everyone eats at least one. Preserve the missing union assumption and check consistency rather than inventing a unique answer."
    },
    {
      "question": "19",
      "note": "NAND controller diagram has complemented feedback and P-input labels. Inspect gates and wiring visually; do not trust OCR stripped bars."
    },
    {
      "question": "22",
      "note": "Precedence diagram visibly directs S6 toward S4 and S5, rather than arrows into S6. Do not flip the bottom arrows to fit a familiar fork/join pattern."
    },
    {
      "question": "23–24",
      "note": "Shared schema startsp13 and continuesp14. Both secondary texts contain cao/cno and sdaddr/saddr transcription differences; record explicit consistent interpretation, do not treat typos as new attributes."
    },
    {
      "question": "28",
      "note": "Set braces are malformed in text extraction; the two-element semigroup is printed as {p,q} and parts(a)/(b) remain separate proof leaves."
    }
